 "grid_note": "HOW THE CELLS WERE LOCATED, in the method T-0532 set for this domain. The 39 vertical rules were fitted as a single pitch off the empty right-hand columns of the same image and the fit was CHECKED AGAINST THE PRINTED HEADING \u2014 column 1 must be 'Under 5', column 14 the FEMALES' 'Under 5', column 27 'Under 10' under FREE COLORED MALES \u2014 before any cell was read. On 33S7-9YYJ-6J the first fit was one column out and the heading is what caught it. The ruled lines were fitted the same way and checked against the names, and the fit was then drawn back over the image and inspected, so a mark is assigned to a column and a line by the grid rather than by eye. Nothing here is an OCR output.",
 "cells_state": "read_partly_reconciled",
 "cells_note": "Twenty-four of the twenty-six free-white columns balance against the figures the enumerator wrote at the foot of this sheet and are committed. TWO DO NOT and are NOT committed: free white males Under 5 (read 18, printed 11) and 5 under 10 (read 10, printed 9). Their readings stay in `cells_first_pass` as the evidence of what is on the page and are absent from `cells`. The residual is not distributed and no line was altered to close a column. Two printed totals had to be re-read before the rest would close: 20 under 30 is 29, not 20 \u2014 the second digit is a 9 whose descender falls below the ruled line \u2014 and free white females Under 5 is 14, not 1, which is exactly what the thirty-one lines sum to. The whole FREE COLORED PERSONS block is unfilled with no total written under it.",
