 "printed_page_note": "The top-right corner where the book's printed page number is struck falls outside the exposure \u2014 the sheet's right edge and the film's black surround are what the corner holds, and no number is on the image. The printed heading's own '(p. 4.)' is the FORM's plate marker, not the book's page, and is not read as one. It is not inferred from the sorted filename order either: group 1 runs 221, 231, 228, 206, 222, 234, 225, 219, 229, ?, 210, 215, 226, 238, so that order is not the book's. It stays unknown, and T-0504's serial fingerprint is the route that can place it.",
 "largest_household_note": "Line 1 carries 11 free white males 20 under 30 and 8 free white males 30 under 40 on one line \u2014 nineteen men, no women under 40, no children. That is a boarding house or a works crew rather than a family, and it is most of why the 30-under-40 column totals 21 on a sheet of 31 households. It is recorded as read; it is not interpreted here and it is not a claim, because a cell reading carries no quote.",
